From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:14:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 62/62] kk: skip a Metal build whose MSL was interrupted twice
 (known-fail list)

iOS ends MTLCompilerService at its 150 MB memory limit, and a library
build then fails with the compiler service interrupted after Metal's own
retries. Red Dead Redemption 2 asked for the same three pipelines again and
again, each failing after 34 to 47 s of compiling, 4 times a run, while
the service was killed 13 to 15 times.

A build (render or compute, any step) that fails with the compiler service
interrupted appends its full MSL hash to
MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR/kk-known-fail-UUID.txt, UUID the device's
pipelineCacheUUID (the driver build, GPU and MSL version). Once an MSL has
failed so twice, in one launch or across launches, its later builds fail
at once with VK_ERROR_INVALID_SHADER_NV, what the failed builds returned,
and log
  [kk-compile] skip known-fail render|compute msl=... interrupted=N src=... tid=...
The second failure logs "[kk-compile] known-fail ... later builds of it
fail at once". Files of other UUIDs are deleted when the list is read, so
any Mesa change empties it, and a changed MSL has another hash; clearing
the shader cache (Settings > Storage) clears it. Without
MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR the list lasts for the process.
MESA_KK_DEBUG=no_known_fail turns it off: every MSL builds and nothing is
recorded.

The risk: an MSL that would build on a less loaded phone stays skipped
until Mesa changes or the cache is cleared.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-20-kk-msl-size.md
Offered-upstream: no
